.\docs\WORKFLOW.md:226:Runtime setup after approval: use `oaf_website.state_requests.create_app(expected_profile=..., recognition_secret=..., public_origin=...)`. Pass a protected persistent random secret of at least 32 bytes, shared by every worker/restart; no generated startup secret or database-credential reuse is provided. The existing database loader still requires the explicit matching `OAF_ENV`; testing uses its testing-only loader and production remains blocked by the existing deployment gate. Flask startup never creates schema or runs Alembic. Each runtime connection checkout verifies database/user/host/port/PostgreSQL 17 identity and requests SCRAM authentication.
